💡 **SUGGESTION: third copy of the decorator-unwrap loop in this file — let `AppStorageCwd` delegate to `AppOwnedEnv`**

`project_mount_env.dart` now contains three structurally identical unwrap loops: `SessionCwd.sessionCwd`, `AppStorageCwd.appStorageCwd`, and the new `AppOwnedEnv.appOwnedEnv` (same `SecretsExecutionEnv → SessionVarsExecutionEnv → ProjectMountEnv → delegate` chain). The new one is the most general — the other two resolve a *string* where it resolves the *env* — so the duplication can collapse to one line:

```dart
extension AppStorageCwd on ExecutionEnv {
  /// The cwd of the app-owned container underneath the decorator stack.
  String? get appStorageCwd => appOwnedEnv.cwd;
}
```

(`SessionCwd` adds sandbox-specific logic on top, so it can stay, but it can also start from `appOwnedEnv` instead of re-walking.) Then a future decorator added to the boot env stack is taught to one loop, not three — exactly the drift class gh-2004 just paid down in the reset codecs.

